data.problem:
Determine if B = 
\begin{bmatrix}
2 & 1 \\
4 & 2
\end{bmatrix}
is invertible by three methods: pivots, determinant, and nonzero null-vector.

For what value(s) of c is the matrix A = 
\begin{bmatrix}
1 & c \\
4 & 2
\end{bmatrix}
singular? For the remaining values solve Ax = 
\begin{bmatrix}
6 \\
4
\end{bmatrix}.
